1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,960
Hey there, chess kids!

2
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,901
Fun Master Mike here.

3
00:00:10,901 --> 00:00:17,385
And today we're going to be covering files, ranks and square names.

4
00:00:17,385 --> 00:00:20,602
What, squares have names?!

5
00:00:20,602 --> 00:00:24,776
Well, yes — in chess they do!

6
00:00:24,776 --> 00:00:28,929
First, we need to learn about ranks.

7
00:00:28,929 --> 00:00:33,857
You can think of ranks as floors in a building.

8
00:00:33,857 --> 00:00:39,799
Ranks have numbers, from 1 to 8, going up the side.

9
00:00:39,799 --> 00:00:43,838
A line of squares that goes side to side…

10
00:00:43,838 --> 00:00:46,270
…is called a rank.

11
00:00:46,270 --> 00:00:50,962
This is the first rank, like the first floor.

12
00:00:50,962 --> 00:00:54,719
White's back-rank pieces start here.

13
00:00:54,719 --> 00:00:58,995
This is the eighth rank, the top floor.

14
00:00:58,995 --> 00:01:02,883
Black's back-rank pieces start here.

15
00:01:02,883 --> 00:01:07,683
Watch the rook slide side to side.

16
00:01:07,683 --> 00:01:15,970
Which rank is it on?

17
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:18,770
The fourth rank!

18
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:22,552
Next, let's learn about files.

19
00:01:22,552 --> 00:01:28,085
Files have letters, from a to h, along the bottom.

20
00:01:28,085 --> 00:01:32,275
A line of squares that goes up and down…

21
00:01:32,275 --> 00:01:34,693
…is called a file.

22
00:01:34,693 --> 00:01:37,265
This is the a-file.

23
00:01:37,265 --> 00:01:41,478
Every square in this line is on the a-file.

24
00:01:41,478 --> 00:01:44,078
This is the e-file.

25
00:01:44,078 --> 00:01:49,405
A file goes up and down, like a single-file line!

26
00:01:49,405 --> 00:01:54,005
Watch the rook slide up and down.

27
00:01:54,005 --> 00:01:56,829
It stays on the e-file!

28
00:01:56,829 --> 00:02:00,067
Now the rook slides sideways…

29
00:02:00,067 --> 00:02:08,644
Which file is it on now?

30
00:02:08,644 --> 00:02:11,444
The c-file!

31
00:02:11,444 --> 00:02:18,124
Stand up! Ranks go side to side!

32
00:02:18,124 --> 00:02:23,649
Files go up and down!

33
00:02:23,649 --> 00:02:27,649
Now for the big idea: square names!

34
00:02:27,649 --> 00:02:31,953
You have a first name and a last name.

35
00:02:31,953 --> 00:02:34,816
Every square does too!

36
00:02:34,816 --> 00:02:40,411
Where a file and a rank cross, you find one square.

37
00:02:40,411 --> 00:02:44,510
Its first name is the letter: e.

38
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:48,925
Its last name is the number: 4.

39
00:02:48,925 --> 00:02:52,661
Put them together: e4!

40
00:02:52,661 --> 00:02:56,072
Letter first, then number.

41
00:02:56,072 --> 00:03:02,352
Say it with me: letter first, then number!

42
00:03:02,352 --> 00:03:07,176
What if we say the number first: {4e}?

43
00:03:07,176 --> 00:03:12,401
No! Letter first, then number: e4!

44
00:03:12,401 --> 00:03:15,863
Let's try a corner square.

45
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:20,302
Look down. The first name is a.

46
00:03:20,302 --> 00:03:24,966
Look across. The last name is 1.

47
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:27,872
This square is a1!

48
00:03:27,872 --> 00:03:32,093
One more! Look down: c.

49
00:03:32,093 --> 00:03:35,613
Look across: 6.

50
00:03:35,613 --> 00:03:38,765
This square is c6!

51
00:03:38,765 --> 00:03:43,509
Chess players call square names coordinates.

52
00:03:43,509 --> 00:03:47,866
Every piece stands on a square with a name.

53
00:03:47,866 --> 00:03:51,569
The white king starts on e1.

54
00:03:51,569 --> 00:03:55,351
The black queen starts on d8.

55
00:03:55,351 --> 00:03:57,973
Find the d-file.

56
00:03:57,973 --> 00:04:00,987
Go up to the eighth rank.

57
00:04:00,987 --> 00:04:03,900
There it is: d8!

58
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:08,563
White's pawn moves from e2 to e4.

59
00:04:08,563 --> 00:04:12,697
In a tournament, you write down your moves.

60
00:04:12,697 --> 00:04:15,586
That is called notation.

61
00:04:15,586 --> 00:04:20,400
When a pawn moves, write the square it moves to.

62
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:24,021
This move is written e4.

63
00:04:24,021 --> 00:04:28,097
Tournament tip! When you play Black…

64
00:04:28,097 --> 00:04:32,497
…you sit on the other side of the board.

65
00:04:32,497 --> 00:04:35,964
Now the a-file is on your right.

66
00:04:35,964 --> 00:04:39,632
The eighth rank is closest to you.

67
00:04:39,632 --> 00:04:43,060
But square names never change!

68
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:46,460
e4 is still e4!

69
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:51,361
Black's pawn moves from e7 to e5.

70
00:04:51,361 --> 00:04:56,961
You write e5.

71
00:04:56,961 --> 00:05:09,119
Your turn! Say this square's name out loud.

72
00:05:09,119 --> 00:05:14,882
Look down: f. Look across: 3.

73
00:05:14,882 --> 00:05:17,482
It's f3!

74
00:05:17,482 --> 00:05:28,088
What is this square's name?

75
00:05:28,088 --> 00:05:33,851
Look down: d. Look across: 7.

76
00:05:33,851 --> 00:05:36,451
It's d7!

77
00:05:36,451 --> 00:05:49,140
Now find b6. Point to it!

78
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,758
Find the b-file.

79
00:05:51,758 --> 00:05:54,993
Go up to the sixth rank.

80
00:05:54,993 --> 00:05:58,184
There it is: b6!

81
00:05:58,184 --> 00:06:00,493
Let's review!

82
00:06:00,493 --> 00:06:04,911
Ranks go…

83
00:06:04,911 --> 00:06:08,997
…side to side! Ranks have numbers.

84
00:06:08,997 --> 00:06:13,240
Files go…

85
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:16,987
…up and down! Files have letters.

86
00:06:16,987 --> 00:06:20,104
First name: the letter.

87
00:06:20,104 --> 00:06:23,319
Last name: the number.

88
00:06:23,319 --> 00:06:27,005
Square names are called coordinates.

89
00:06:27,005 --> 00:06:31,405
Now you can name every square on the board!

90
00:06:31,405 --> 00:06:35,005
Great work, chess kids!
